# Commands in Russian: прочита́й!
subtitle: "Tell a friend to get something done, to keep at it, or not to do it in Russian: прочита́й or чита́й, позвони́, не открыва́й, не забу́дь, and дава́й посмо́трим."
tags: ["russian","russian imperative","russian aspect","commands","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/imperatives","grammar/aspect"]
thumb: "band \"Read it, or read ALL of it?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"I must in Russian: я до́лжен","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/67-russian-must.cast"}

## Commands in Russian: прочита́й!
level: basic

